<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Carlsberg 1995/96 profit seen up.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Carlsberg 1995/96 profit seen up.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>In a Reuter poll issued on Friday, eight analysts forecast that Danish brewery Carlsberg A/S would achieve its own growth rates for 1995/96, with profits up on the previous year.</p>
<p>The panel foresaw average rises in operating profits at 1.264 billion crowns, five percent better than in 1994/95, with net profit after minorities some two percent up at 1.020 billion crowns on six percent higher 14.2 billion crown turnover.</p>
<p>Carlsberg posted 1.003 billion crown net profits after minorities for 1994/95. The brewery announces its 1995/96 result on Monday November 25. --Jorn Nurkka, Cop newsroom +45-33969652</p>
